A previous go-round on Lojban poetry suggested
(and argued convincingly for) that Lojban meter
was a matter of *stressed* syllables per line,
the unstressed ones being permitted to run to
(almost, I suppose) any length. By that standard
we have (assuming words after {zo} are stressed)
2-2-3, 1-2-3, 1-0-2.  I assume there are some
further stress rules that bring this more into
line, but it is still not quite on.






           

